          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: добавлять",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "добавлять (dobavlyát) — \"to add\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В суп я добавил немного соли. V sup ya dobávil nemnógo sóli. I added a little salt to the soup."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective добавить (dobávit), добавлю. It takes the accusative, or the genitive for \"some\": добавить сахару."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "добавлять (dobavlyát) is built on до- and an old verb бавить \"to make, to keep busy\", as in забава \"amusement\"; the link is usually traced, and EtymDB lists no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
